@node Stores
@section Stores
@cindex store

A @dfn{store} is the on-disk Beads database for one project.  It lives
under a @file{.beads/} directory at the project root; @command{bd init}
creates it.  The default engine is embedded Dolt, which keeps each
project's data under @file{.beads/embeddeddolt/} with filesystem-level
isolation, so two checkouts never share a database by accident.  A store
can also be served by a shared Dolt server; @code{beads.el} then scopes
every command with @command{--directory} so a shared server routes to the
intended project (@pxref{Store Scoping}).

@node Issues
@section Issues
@cindex issue
@cindex issue id

An @dfn{issue} is the unit of work: a ticket with a stable id, a title, a
Markdown description, a status, a priority, a type, an assignee, labels,
dependencies, and a comment thread.  Issue ids are short base-36 hashes
with a project prefix, for example @code{bd-42}; @code{beads.el} matches
them anywhere for eldoc previews.

@table @asis
@item Status
One of @code{open}, @code{in_progress}, @code{blocked}, @code{closed},
and the other states @command{bd} understands.
@item Priority
@code{0} (Critical) through @code{4} (Backlog).
@item Type
@code{bug}, @code{feature}, @code{task}, @code{epic}, @code{chore}, and
friends.
@item Labels
Free-form tags shared across issues.
@end table

@node Dependency Model
@section Dependency Model
@cindex dependency
@cindex blocks
@cindex relates to

A @dfn{dependency} is a directed edge between two issues that records
how one constrains the other.  The common kinds are @code{blocks} (the
source cannot proceed until the target is done), @code{relates_to} (a
soft, bidirectional association), and parent/child links that make an
issue a child of an epic.  Dependencies drive the ready and blocked
views: an issue is @dfn{ready} when nothing blocks it and @dfn{blocked}
when at least one dependency does.

@node Molecules and Formulas
@section Molecules and Formulas
@cindex formula
@cindex molecule
@cindex epic

A @dfn{formula} is a reusable, parameterized template (authored as TOML)
that expands into a connected graph of issues.  Pouring a formula
instantiates it into a @dfn{molecule}: the concrete graph of issues,
dependencies, and labels created in a store.  Molecules make multi-step
work such as release checklists or a whole feature plan repeatable.  An
@dfn{epic} is an issue that parents other issues; epics compose with
molecules and are surfaced by the epic-health views.
